@startuml CL06_Geometry
!include _style.iuml
title CL-06  Core.Geometry — site, operating window, coordinates, lens projection, working area, ROI

package "NINAAllskySafetyMonitor.Core.Geometry" {
  class SiteLocationResolver {
    -profileSource : ISiteLocationSource
    -fallback : Func<SiteSettings>
    +Resolve() : SiteLocation
    .. REQ-04 ..
  }
  class OperatingWindow {
    -astro : IAstroCalculator
    +Evaluate(site, nowUtc, sunAltitudeLimitDeg) : ConditionCheck
    .. REQ-08 REQ-09 REQ-10 ..
  }
  class CoordinateConverter <<static>> {
    +LocalSiderealDeg(utc, longitudeDeg) : double
    +ToHorizontal(raHours, decDeg, epoch, site, utc) : HorizontalCoordinate
    +ToEquatorial(h, site, utc, epoch) : (double, double)
    .. REQ-24 ..
  }
  class SkyGeometry <<static>> {
    +SeparationDeg(a, b : HorizontalCoordinate) : double
    +Destination(start, bearingDeg, distanceDeg) : HorizontalCoordinate
    +Normalise(deg) : double
  }
  class LensCalibration <<record>> {
    +CentreX : double
    +CentreY : double
    +NorthRotationDeg : double
    +EastIsClockwise : bool
    +RadialCoefficients : double[]
    +StarsMatched : int
    +RmsErrorPx : double
    +RmsErrorDeg : double
    +CalibratedUtc : DateTime
    +Manual : bool
    .. REQ-19 ..
  }
  class LensProjection {
    -lens : LensCalibration
    +ToPixel(h : HorizontalCoordinate) : PixelPoint
    +ToHorizontal(p : PixelPoint) : HorizontalCoordinate
    +HorizonRadiusPx : double
    +{static} Approximate(width, height) : LensCalibration
    +{static} FromHorizonRadius(cx, cy, radiusPx, northDeg, eastClockwise) : LensCalibration
    .. REQ-19 REQ-24 ..
  }
  class WorkingAreaDefinition <<record>> {
    +CentreAltDeg = 75
    +CentreAzDeg = 180
    +RadiusDeg = 60
    +Outline : IReadOnlyList<PixelPoint>
    .. REQ-22 REQ-57 ..
  }
  class WorkingArea {
    -definition : WorkingAreaDefinition
    -projection : LensProjection?
    +Contains(h : HorizontalCoordinate) : bool
    ~{static} InsidePolygon(p, polygon) : bool
    .. REQ-22 REQ-25 ..
  }
  class MountStateInterpreter {
    +WhyUnusable(m : MountState?) : string?
    +IsUsableForRoi(m : MountState?) : bool
    .. REQ-07 REQ-26 ..
  }
  class RoiCalculator {
    -astro : IAstroCalculator
    -interpreter : MountStateInterpreter
    +CalculateCentre(m : MountState?, site, nowUtc) : (HorizontalCoordinate? Centre, string? Unusable)
    .. REQ-06 REQ-23 REQ-24 REQ-26 ..
  }
  class RoiBuilder {
    +Build(centre?, unusableReason?, radiusDeg, minInsideFraction, area : WorkingArea) : RegionOfInterest
    ~{static} InsideFraction(centre, radiusDeg, area) : double
    .. REQ-23 REQ-25 REQ-26 REQ-58 ..
  }
}

LensProjection --> LensCalibration
WorkingArea --> WorkingAreaDefinition
WorkingArea --> LensProjection
WorkingArea ..> SkyGeometry
RoiCalculator --> MountStateInterpreter
RoiBuilder ..> WorkingArea
RoiBuilder ..> SkyGeometry
CoordinateConverter ..> SkyGeometry

note bottom of SiteLocationResolver
  Uses the NINA profile location; a profile
  at 0°, 0° or out of range counts as unset,
  so the configured location is used.
end note
note bottom of RoiCalculator
  Centre is always computed from RA/Dec (IAstroCalculator →
  CoordinateConverter: IAU GMST, J2000 precessed to the date,
  about 0.01°). The mount-reported Alt/Az go to the decision log
  for diagnostics only (REQ-06). No centre when the mount is not
  usable, with the reason ("Mount parked", …).
end note
note bottom of RoiBuilder
  The ROI is judged on the sky: InsideFraction samples 400
  points spread over the 15° circle and tests each with
  WorkingArea.Contains. No usable mount position (REQ-26), or
  less than MinInsideFraction inside (REQ-58): the whole working
  area is used, and RegionOfInterest.Note says why. The pixel
  mask for cloud detection is built in slice 6.
end note
note bottom of LensProjection
  r = c1·z + c2·z² + c3·z³ (z = zenith distance, radians).
  Until calibrated: Approximate() from the image size, or a
  hand-entered model (Manual = true). Calibrated (slice 5b):
  fitted to catalogue stars by LensFitter (CL-09).
end note
@enduml
